 "Opus 5.5 played C6 and lost 4.4 points, turning +0.3 into -4.1. The engine wanted D7, the point White took next. After that White held the upper side and Black had to fight for the rest."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "The decisive move. With the lead at -5.9, Opus 5.5 played D4 and lost 19.1 points, leaving the lead at -25.0. The engine's choice was F7, which Black needed at every turn after this. Black had a wall on row 6 and White's stones sat on the fourth row. The game was effectively lost here."}, {"turn": 36, "text": "White answered with F5 and lost 17.8 points, moving the lead from -33.5 to -15.8. This was a big gift. Black's stones at G6 and H6 had cut into the right side, and for a moment the game looked closer."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "Opus 5.5 played J7 and lost 21.4 points, the worst move of the game. The lead fell from -15.8 to -37.2, erasing everything White had just given back. The engine wanted H9."}, {"turn": 38, "text": "White's J5 lost 19.5 points, bringing the lead from -37.2 to -17.7. The 12k was playing loosely too, but with the margin this large, even a 19.5-point slip could not put Black ahead, and Opus 5.5 resigned soon after."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py and count.py only parse a pasted board and compute group liberties and area counts of the current position; the other commands cat/tail games.md and append a game log entry, so nothing chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}